<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin von Neurath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1956">1956</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin von Neurath was a German diplomat who served as foreign minister from 1932 to 1938 and then as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-protector">Reich Protector</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> from 1939. Considered too lenient by Hitler, he was replaced in practice by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a> in 1941. At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> he was convicted of war crimes and sentenced to fifteen years, but was released early in 1954.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-neurath.jpg" alt="Konstantin von Neurath" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Sennecke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KonstantinVonNeurath1933_(cropped).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
